// Devices, pairing, push targets and notification preferences (design §37
// §7.2, §7.4; AP0 Task 2).
//
// A phone (or a desktop) is a device credential of a user principal, not a
// principal of its own (D434). A signed-in user creates a short-lived
// pairing here; the phone redeems it at the Loams gateway's OAuth token
// endpoint, not through an RPC of this service:
//
//   POST {issuer}/api/v1/oauth/token
//     grant_type=urn:loams:params:oauth:grant-type:pairing   (RFC 6749 §4.5)
//     code=<from the QR> | user_code=<8 digits typed>         (exactly one)
//     client_id=loams-ios | loams-android
//     device_name, platform, decision_jwk, [key attestation]
//     DPoP: <proof>                                           (RFC 9449)
//   → {access_token, token_type: "DPoP", expires_in, refresh_token, device_id}
//
